From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew <andrew@localhost>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] module-droid-hidl: guard dbus_done against a null
 dbus_protocol

Found 2026-09-11 testing a freshly-built pulseaudio-modules-droid on
real hardware where the droid HAL open legitimately fails (EINVAL - no
audio DSP running behind it on that particular boot): with
module-droid-card unable to open the HAL, module-droid-hidl's own
pa__init() correctly detects this (its DROID_HW_HANDLE/
DROID_SET_PARAMETERS/DROID_GET_PARAMETERS pa_shared_get() lookups all
fail - "Couldn't get hw module functions, is module-droid-card
loaded?") and jumps to its fail: label *before* ever calling
dbus_init(u). That label unconditionally calls pa__done(), which
unconditionally calls dbus_done(u).

u is allocated with pa_xnew0(), so u->dbus_protocol is still NULL at
that point - dbus_init() is the only place that sets it, and it never
ran. dbus_done() then calls
pa_dbus_protocol_unregister_extension(NULL, ...) unconditionally,
which asserts inside PulseAudio core:

    E: [pulseaudio] droid-util.c: Failed to open audio hw device : Invalid argument (22).
    E: [pulseaudio] module.c: Failed to load module "module-droid-card" ...: initialization failed.
    E: [pulseaudio] module-droid-hidl.c: Couldn't get hw module functions, is module-droid-card loaded?
    E: [pulseaudio] protocol-dbus.c: Assertion 'p' failed at .../protocol-dbus.c:1116, function pa_dbus_protocol_unregister_extension(). Aborting.
    systemd[1]: pulseaudio.service: Main process exited, code=dumped, status=6/ABRT

So a HAL-open failure that should just mean "no droid card, and
module-droid-hidl declines to load too" instead takes the whole
daemon down - unrelated to and much more disruptive than the actual
failure. This is a real upstream bug, not LuneOS-specific: it fires
whenever the droid HAL open fails for any reason on any device using
this module, not just on a board with no DSP behind it.

Guard the same way module-droid-card's own park_profile() null check
does - by checking the thing that dbus_init() is the sole setter of
before touching it.

Signed-off-by: Andrew <andrew@localhost>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/hidl/module-droid-hidl.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hidl/module-droid-hidl.c b/src/hidl/module-droid-hidl.c
--- a/src/hidl/module-droid-hidl.c
+++ b/src/hidl/module-droid-hidl.c
@@ -167,6 +167,18 @@ static void dbus_init(struct userdata *u) {
 static void dbus_done(struct userdata *u) {
     pa_assert(u);
 
+    /* pa__init() jumps to its fail: label, which unconditionally calls
+     * pa__done() -> dbus_done(), on several checks that run before
+     * dbus_init() (e.g. the DROID_HW_HANDLE shared-value lookup, which
+     * fails whenever module-droid-card did not load - this project's own
+     * case, and in general any device where the droid HAL open fails).
+     * u is pa_xnew0()'d, so u->dbus_protocol is still NULL in that case,
+     * and unregistering against a NULL protocol asserts inside
+     * pulseaudio core (protocol-dbus.c: Assertion 'p' failed ... Aborting),
+     * taking the whole daemon down instead of just failing this module. */
+    if (!u->dbus_protocol)
+        return;
+
     pa_dbus_protocol_unregister_extension(u->dbus_protocol, AUDIOSYSTEM_PASSTHROUGH_IFACE);
     pa_dbus_protocol_remove_interface(u->dbus_protocol, AUDIOSYSTEM_PASSTHROUGH_PATH, passthrough_info.name);
     pa_dbus_protocol_unref(u->dbus_protocol);
-- 
